  "thermal_via_policy": "R1-R3 DEVELOPMENT REVIEW: 0.5 mm copper / 0.2 mm finished drill, 0.15 mm nominal annular ring. Existing front/back tenting retained; exposed-pad F.Mask opens the top. Tenting is not a complete seal and does not close solder-wicking risk under the unchanged full paste apertures. Supplier stencil and via process review is a PRE-ORDER gate; no filled/plugged/capped process or cost is adopted. JLC capability geometry read 2026-11-09: preferred 0.2 mm hole; 0.15 mm diameter-minus-hole preferred; 0.2 mm hole-to-hole minimum. See https://jlcpcb.com/capabilities/Capab and https://jlcpcb.com/blog/five-via-finishes (updated 2026-04-08): via-in-pad/exposed-side/near-mask-opening ink-plug restrictions; epoxy/copper fill requires explicit process selection. Thermal rating remains unmeasured.",
  "back_spreading_constraints": "EF_IN B.Cu neck/strip clears R24/C1/C37 and stops at x9.3 to preserve the short C1-to-C2 VBUS_IN path. VBUS_OUT B.Cu island leaves R27/R11/R13/C36 non-output pads outside its reserved region. These supplement the unchanged main F.Cu path; widths/areas do not independently establish 5 A or thermal acceptance.",
